// @check
// @error operator `+` never dispatches: `self` is a TYPE PARAMETER, so whether it fires is decided at each site — and every `+` site in this program took the language's own lowering. Annotate `self` with the object type the operator is for, or remove the declaration
// GRADUATED from `silent-class-inventory` D491 — the last binary operator declaration
// that was silently ignored, and the layer it is answered at is neither of the two the
// row's parent (#2007) refuted.
//
// D425's `binOpDeadSelf` refuses a declaration whose `self` can never be an object and
// SUBTRACTS the hole, correctly: `function "+"<T>(self: T, other: T)` is silent at an i32
// site and DISPATCHES at an object one, so no DECLARATION-site rule is right for both.
// #2007 then refuted the CALL-site rule too — an unconstrained `T` is assignable from
// everything, so a site reject that catches `a + b` at i32 also refuses
// `function unrelated(): i32 { return 40 + 2 }` in another function.
//
// Both refutations hold. What neither covers is that the checker VISITS EVERY SITE before
// `checkProgram` returns. `checkBinary`'s `if odsp is TyObj` gate already decides, per
// site, whether a user operator could fire; banking that decision by operator NAME and
// reading it back at the end of the pass answers the whole-program question neither end
// can: a hole-`self` declaration that NO site dispatched to, while at least one site took
// the built-in, is a declaration that never fires. Positioned at the declaration, at
// `vl check`, where an editor can show it.
//
// The MONOMORPHIZER, which the row named as the remaining home, is not it — and the row's
// stated mechanism there is false. Probed: `T` is never pinned at `i32`, because
// `dispatchRewrite` declines to rewrite `a + b` into a call, so `monoInstantiate` is never
// entered and the declaration is replaced by a `() -> void` prune stub. Its available
// discriminator is "instantiated at all", not "pinned at i32 versus at V" — and it fires
// after `vl check` has already said the file is fine.
//
// The `at least one site declined` half is load-bearing: `d471_pin_typaram` declares the
// same operator with NO `a op b` site anywhere and must keep running. Nothing was silently
// ignored there — there was nothing to ignore, which is the linter's sentence, not this
// one's.
function "+"<T>(self: T, other: T): i32 {
  return 99
}

const a: i32 = 7
const b: i32 = 1
print(a + b)
